@* Failback hint under a secret field: the stored value is DPAPI-protected for another
   Windows user/PC (settings.json was copied from elsewhere), so it bound as empty and the
   only fix is to re-enter it. Renders nothing while the path decrypts fine. The path is the
   configuration spelling ("prosim:apiKey") — the same string SecretProtector.SecretPaths
   registers, so a typo here simply never shows rather than throwing. *@

@if (SecretProtector.Unreadable.Contains(Path))
{
    <div class="field-hint field-hint-warn">
        Stored key can't be decrypted on this PC/user (settings copied from elsewhere) — re-enter it and save.
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The <c>section:key</c> config path of the secret this hint watches.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Path { get; set; } = "";
}
